// **RT2-2b: the reference renderer** (`--reference-render=N`).
//
// A path tracer at a fixed pose, accumulated into a running mean one path per
// pixel per frame, with none of the real-time chain's tools for hiding noise:
// no resolve, no colour box, no firefly clamp, no history beyond the mean, no
// TAA. Its job is to say which picture is right, so it must not share the
// shortcuts it judges. From the shared header it takes only data -- the
// scene's bindings and the ray structure -- and walks the structure itself:
// the shared traversal carries real-time decisions (thin members fading out
// with distance, a lamp's ray let through its own fitting) that the reference
// must not inherit. It does its own shading: the material evaluated in full at
// every vertex, the sky and the glowing surfaces reached by the paths
// themselves, and every light sampled by next-event estimation.
//
// **The material is the lit shader's, evaluated exactly** -- the definition the
// frame is judged against, not a second opinion about it: GGX (anisotropic
// where the material asks) with its Smith-Schlick geometry term, Schlick
// Fresnel, the diffuse weighted by (1 - F)(1 - metallic) and wrapped where the
// material asks, the clearcoat taking its share first, the sheen on top; the
// same 0.045 floor on roughness the frame applies, the same normal map through
// the same tangent frame (TangentFrameOf, from the triangle's edges where the
// frame uses the screen's derivatives -- the same frame on a flat triangle),
// the same parallax march, the same macro variation, and terrain's four layers
// through its weight map with the cliff projection. What it leaves out is what
// the frame does to *hide* sampling, never what the material is: no filtered
// roughness (WR-13) -- the reference resolves the pixel by averaging -- and no
// widened lobe for a sized lamp, whose real shape step 3 samples.
//
// **The Smith term is the exact one** (owner, 2026-10-13): the
// height-correlated masking-shadowing of the GGX microsurface (Heitz 2014),
// anisotropic where the lobe is, which is what Unreal, Frostbite and Filament
// ship for every light. The frame carries two approximations of it -- the
// light loop's Schlick remap k = (r+1)^2/8, made for point lamps and darker
// than the truth at a grazing view, and the reflections' k = r^2/2 in the
// EnvBRDF table -- and the reference judges both rather than adopting either;
// RT2-21b moves the frame onto this one. Shown to the owner on the garage's
// wet floor: the car's reflection in the puddles is 58% brighter with it.
//
// **Albedo is held to [0, 1]** (review, 2026-10-13), as the G-buffer's UNORM
// lane holds it; the forward loop does not, and an albedo above one (a
// macro-brightened texel) is light from nowhere. (The review also found the
// light loop's GGX capping polished peaks below roughness 0.065 through the
// floor on its divisor; that is fixed in DistributionGGX itself, owner's OK
// 2026-10-13.)
//
// **GGX's distribution in the form that keeps its precision** (step 4's
// furnace). DistributionGGX builds its divisor from 1 - (N.H)^2, which in
// float cancels near the peak: at roughness 0.045 the peak itself is off by
// up to 3%, and a mirror sphere under a uniform sky read 2% dark in places,
// because the sampler's density used the other form and the two no longer
// divided out. The reference evaluates D through the half vector's tangent
// components (DistributionGGXAniso at equal widths -- the same function,
// without the cancellation) for the material and the density alike.
//
// **Textures at the ray's footprint** (a ray cone, Akenine-Moller et al. 2021):
// the cone starts at the pixel's angle and grows with the distance travelled;
// the level is the cone's width over the hit's slope against the triangle's
// texel density. The pixel itself is already averaged by the jittered samples,
// so the cone only has to cover the spacing between them: its angle is the
// pixel's over the square root of the samples the mean is heading for, never
// below an eighth of it (pbrt-v4's rule). It does not widen at a bounce: the
// lobe is integrated by the paths, and widening for it would filter twice.
// Up close the level is zero; at a distance it saves fetches without changing
// what the average converges to, except through the mips' own averaging of
// normals and roughness. Alpha is read at level zero always: coverage is a
// threshold, and a threshold of an average is not the average coverage.
//
// **Glass** (owner, 2026-10-13): blended materials join the structure only in
// this mode, on a mask bit no other ray carries (RV_RAY_MASK_TRANSMISSIVE).
// A pane is thin glass: its opacity (the blend alpha) is the share that is
// ordinary surface, shaded with the material as anything else; the clear rest
// reflects by the dielectric's Fresnel through the GGX lobe at the pane's
// roughness and passes the remainder straight through. Untinted, because the
// frame's glass has no tint to judge yet (RT2-31 adds one). A light's ray
// through panes keeps the product of their transmittances -- exact for thin
// glass, in any order, provided no crossing is counted twice, which is checked
// here rather than left to the hardware.
//
// **Water** (owner, 2026-10-13: "the engine's water, traced"). A body of water
// joins the structure only in this mode, as its displaced surface (written once
// by water_positions.rvshader -- the clock stands still -- with the per-vertex
// normal, Jacobian and crest the water pass's vertex stage hands its
// fragments), on its own mask bit. At a hit the surface is the water pass's:
// the wave normal plus its two detail ripples (faded with distance from the
// camera, as drawn), the wet-crest smoothing, the Cox-Munk roughness that
// grows with the camera's footprint, and the colour from shallow to deep by the
// water behind the surface along the view. Its light is the water's own model:
// the Beckmann lobe about the wind for what the surface reflects; for what
// enters, the refracted ray to the bottom through Beer-Lambert at the
// component's gradient depth, and the lit body colour taking over as that
// transmittance dies. Lights' rays pass through the surface, as the frame's do
// (its water is in no structure), and so does a path once it is under water --
// the frame absorbs along the one refracted ray it traces and nowhere else.
// Two departures, both the frame's arithmetic rather than its intent: the
// light that enters is (1 - F) of what arrives (the frame adds the refracted
// scene at full strength beside a full Fresnel reflection), and the lobe's
// masking is height-correlated, as the owner chose for every lobe. Foam and
// caustics are the water pass's too (owner, 2026-10-15): the crest foam where
// the surface folds, the contact foam where the water meets anything, and the
// trails the pass accumulates, read from the engine's own trail buffer (still
// empty while the clock stands still, as at the scene's first instant); the
// foam whitens and roughens the surface and hides the bottom, and the caustic
// web multiplies what is seen of the bottom, as the frame's traced refraction
// does.
//
// **Lights** (step 3). Every vertex takes one sample of a lamp and one of a
// glowing surface, and every path that scatters can also meet them; the two
// strategies are weighed by Veach's power heuristic (MIS), so each light is
// found by whichever does it better -- a small lamp by its sample, its image
// in a mirror by the path. Lamps have the shapes the frame gives them (spheres,
// capsules) and the frame's total light; glowing surfaces are their own
// triangles. RefLampNee and RefEmitterNee say how each is chosen.
//
// Steps of RT2-2b (2026-10-13): 1 the skeleton, glass, water; 2 the full
// material; 3 the lights (this). The
// baked ambient-occlusion map is ignored on purpose (owner, 2026-10-13): the
// paths compute the occlusion it stands in for. A lamp that also has a glowing
// mesh is counted both ways, as the frame counts it today, until RT2-11 links
// the two (owner, 2026-10-13).

#type vertex
#version 460 core

layout(location = 0) out vec2 v_UV;

void main()
{
	v_UV = vec2((gl_VertexIndex << 1) & 2, gl_VertexIndex & 2);
	gl_Position = vec4(v_UV * 2.0 - 1.0, 0.0, 1.0);
}

#type fragment
#version 460 core

#define RV_TRACE_ONLY
#include "include/pbr_fragment.glsl"
#include "include/view_reconstruction.glsl"
// The water's lobe, which the lit shader includes only in its water variant.
#include "include/water_lobe.glsl"

layout(location = 0) in vec2 v_UV;

// The mean so far: rgb the radiance, a the samples that came back not a
// number (counted, never averaged in -- a reference that hid them would hide
// its own bugs).
layout(set = 3, binding = 0) uniform sampler2D u_ReferencePrevious;

// What only this pass reads at a ray hit: per ray row the record its flag
// names (~0u for none) -- a terrain chunk's layers (LayeredParams, the block
// the layered lit shader reads, with the bindless slots filled), or a body of
// water's dials.
layout(std430, set = 3, binding = 1) readonly buffer ReferenceRowExtra
{
	uint Rows[];
} u_RefRowExtra;

struct RefLayered
{
	vec4  BaseColor[4];
	vec4  EmissiveColor[4];
	vec4  Surface[4];        // metallic, roughness, occlusion, normal scale
	vec4  UvTransform[4];
	vec4  Specular;
	vec4  HeightScale;
	vec4  MacroScale;
	vec4  MacroStrength;
	ivec4 MapFlags;
	vec4  WeightUv;
	uvec4 BaseColorSlots;
	uvec4 NormalSlots;
	uvec4 RoughnessSlots;    // roughness, occlusion, height in r, g, b
	uvec4 WeightSlot;
};

layout(std430, set = 3, binding = 2) readonly buffer ReferenceLayered
{
	RefLayered Records[];
} u_RefLayered;

const int REF_LAYER_ACTIVE = 1 << 15;

// A body of water: the dials as Renderer3D::WaterDraw packs them for the water
// pass (shallow rgb + gradient metres; deep rgb + the clock; height,
// wavelength, choppiness, speed; direction in radians, foam, the previous
// clock, spacing), the per-vertex surface the wave pass wrote (two vec4 a
// vertex: normal + Jacobian, crest), and the detail ripple map's heap slot.
struct RefWater
{
	vec4  Shallow;
	vec4  Deep;
	vec4  Wave;
	vec4  Extra;
	vec4  Size;            // xy the body's rectangle in metres
	uvec2 SurfaceAddress;
	uint  DetailSlot;
	uint  PatternSlot;     // the foam pattern, which the caustic web is also read from
	uint  FoamSlot;        // the trail buffer: r fresh, g residual
	uint  Pad0;
	uint  Pad1;
	uint  Pad2;
};

layout(std430, set = 3, binding = 3) readonly buffer ReferenceWater
{
	RefWater Records[];
} u_RefWater;

// The glowing surfaces (step 3): per ray row its record (~0u for none); per
// glowing instance its world bounding sphere, mean emitted radiance and total
// area, and its run of triangles; per triangle its world corners, the running
// share of the instance's area that ends at it, its primitive and its area.
layout(std430, set = 3, binding = 4) readonly buffer ReferenceRowEmitter
{
	uint Rows[];
} u_RefRowEmitter;

struct RefEmitter
{
	vec4 Sphere;     // xyz centre, w radius
	vec4 Radiance;   // rgb mean emitted radiance, w total area
	uint FirstTriangle;
	uint TriangleCount;
	uint Row;
	uint Pad;
};

layout(std430, set = 3, binding = 5) readonly buffer ReferenceEmitters
{
	RefEmitter Records[];
} u_RefEmitters;

struct RefEmitterTriangle
{
	vec4 P0;   // xyz first corner, w the running area share ending here
	vec4 E1;   // xyz to the second corner, w the primitive (float bits)
	vec4 E2;   // xyz to the third corner, w the area
};

layout(std430, set = 3, binding = 6) readonly buffer ReferenceTriangles
{
	RefEmitterTriangle Records[];
} u_RefTriangles;

layout(push_constant) uniform ReferenceParams
{
	vec4 Projection;   // xy the inverse projection, z one where rows run down (Vulkan), w samples so far
	vec4 Settings;     // x the most bounces, y one where a mean exists to add to, z the samples the mean is heading for, w the debug lane (0 off)
	vec4 CameraRow0;
	vec4 CameraRow1;
	vec4 CameraRow2;
	vec4 CameraPosition;
} u_Ref;

layout(location = 0) out vec4 o_Mean;

// A path above water sees every world: the static and the moving halves and,
// in this mode only, the glass and the water. A light's ray, and a path once
// it is under water, see everything but the water (the header says why).
const uint REF_MASK_DRY = RV_RAY_MASK_STATIC | RV_RAY_MASK_MOVING | RV_RAY_MASK_TRANSMISSIVE;
const uint REF_MASK_ALL = REF_MASK_DRY | RV_RAY_MASK_WATER;

// Water's refraction ratio, air into water, as the frame's (1 / 1.33).
const float REF_WATER_ETA = 0.7519;

// The frame's floor on roughness (pbr_fragment.glsl, main), part of the
// material as it is defined today; RT2-21c removes it from both.
const float REF_ROUGHNESS_FLOOR = 0.045;

// --- random numbers: PCG, one stream per pixel and sample -------------------

uint g_Rng;

uint RefNext()
{
	const uint state = g_Rng * 747796405u + 2891336453u;
	g_Rng = state;
	const uint word = ((state >> ((state >> 28u) + 4u)) ^ state) * 277803737u;
	return (word >> 22u) ^ word;
}

float RefRandom()
{
	return float(RefNext() >> 8u) * (1.0 / 16777216.0);
}

// The ray cone's angle in radians, the same for every segment of every path.
float g_ConeSpread;

// The camera's forward axis, and what a distance along this segment is worth
// as view depth: the frame measures the water behind the surface as a
// difference of view depths, so a camera ray's distance is scaled by its
// cosine to the axis; any later segment has no view depth and keeps its own.
vec3 g_CameraForward;
float g_ViewDepthScale;

// --- rays ------------------------------------------------------------------

// Off the surface along a normal by a few ULPs of the position (Wachter and
// Binder, Ray Tracing Gems ch. 6): a fixed distance is too much at the camp
// and too little 2 km out on the bridge.
vec3 RefOffset(vec3 p, vec3 n)
{
	const float origin = 1.0 / 32.0;
	const float floatScale = 1.0 / 65536.0;
	const float intScale = 256.0;
	const ivec3 o = ivec3(intScale * n);
	const vec3 pi = vec3(intBitsToFloat(floatBitsToInt(p.x) + (p.x < 0.0 ? -o.x : o.x)),
						 intBitsToFloat(floatBitsToInt(p.y) + (p.y < 0.0 ? -o.y : o.y)),
						 intBitsToFloat(floatBitsToInt(p.z) + (p.z < 0.0 ? -o.z : o.z)));
	return vec3(abs(p.x) < origin ? p.x + floatScale * n.x : pi.x,
				abs(p.y) < origin ? p.y + floatScale * n.y : pi.y,
				abs(p.z) < origin ? p.z + floatScale * n.z : pi.z);
}

// A triangle of an instance: its corners' indices and where on it the ray is.
struct RefTriangle
{
	uint I0, I1, I2;
	vec2 Bary;
};

RefTriangle RefTriangleOf(RayInstance hit, uint primitive, vec2 bary)
{
	RayWords indices = RayWords(hit.IndexAddress);
	RefTriangle t;
	t.I0 = indices.Words[primitive * 3u + 0u];
	t.I1 = indices.Words[primitive * 3u + 1u];
	t.I2 = indices.Words[primitive * 3u + 2u];
	t.Bary = bary;
	return t;
}

// The mesh's own uv at one corner, before any material's tiling.
vec2 RefCornerUv(RayInstance hit, uint index)
{
	RayFloats attributes = RayFloats(hit.AttributeAddress);
	const uint as_ = hit.AttributeStrideWords;
	return vec2(attributes.Floats[index * as_ + 6u], attributes.Floats[index * as_ + 7u]);
}

vec2 RefUv(RayInstance hit, GpuMaterial material, RefTriangle t)
{
	const float w0 = 1.0 - t.Bary.x - t.Bary.y;
	const vec2 uv = RefCornerUv(hit, t.I0) * w0 + RefCornerUv(hit, t.I1) * t.Bary.x
				  + RefCornerUv(hit, t.I2) * t.Bary.y;
	return uv * material.UvTransform.xy + material.UvTransform.zw;
}

// The material's coverage at a point: the blend alpha for glass, the cutout's
// alpha for a masked surface. The base colour map's alpha at level zero.
float RefAlpha(RayInstance hit, GpuMaterial material, RefTriangle t)
{
	float alpha = hit.BaseColor.a;
	if ((material.MapFlags & MAP_BASE_COLOR) != 0)
		alpha *= textureLod(u_Textures[nonuniformEXT(material.Maps0.x)], RefUv(hit, material, t), 0.0).a;
	return alpha;
}

// A pane's clear share reflects 0.08 x specular at normal incidence, its
// specular map read at level zero: one value for the path that meets the pane
// and the light ray that crosses it, so the two agree on what passes.
float RefPaneF0(RayInstance hit, GpuMaterial material, RefTriangle t)
{
	float specular = material.Specular;
	if ((material.MapFlags & MAP_SPECULAR) != 0)
		specular *= textureLod(u_Textures[nonuniformEXT(material.Maps1.z)], RefUv(hit, material, t), 0.0).r;
	return 0.08 * clamp(specular, 0.0, 1.0);
}

// The glow at a point of an instance -- its emissive times its map, at level
// zero -- read the same way by a path that meets it and by a light sample
// aimed at it, so the two strategies weigh the same thing.
vec3 RefEmission(uint row, uint primitive, vec2 bary)
{
	const RayInstance hit = u_RayInstances.Instances[row];
	const GpuMaterial material = u_Materials.Materials[hit.MaterialIndex];
	vec3 glow = hit.EmissiveColor.rgb;
	if ((material.MapFlags & MAP_EMISSIVE) != 0)
		glow *= textureLod(u_Textures[nonuniformEXT(material.Maps0.w)],
						   RefUv(hit, material, RefTriangleOf(hit, primitive, bary)), 0.0).rgb;
	return glow;
}

// Whether a candidate is a surface for a ray looking for the nearest one.
// Glass is; a cutout is where its alpha clears the cutoff; anything else in a
// non-opaque instance (a fitting) is solid. No distance fade, no fitting let
// through: those are the frame's choices, not the scene's.
bool RefCandidateIsSurface(rayQueryEXT q)
{
	const uint instance = uint(rayQueryGetIntersectionInstanceCustomIndexEXT(q, false));
	RayInstance hit = u_RayInstances.Instances[instance];
	if ((hit.Flags & RAY_INSTANCE_TRANSMISSIVE) != 0u)
		return true;
	if ((hit.Flags & RAY_INSTANCE_MASKED) == 0u)
		return true;
	const GpuMaterial material = u_Materials.Materials[hit.MaterialIndex];
	const RefTriangle t = RefTriangleOf(hit, uint(rayQueryGetIntersectionPrimitiveIndexEXT(q, false)),
										rayQueryGetIntersectionBarycentricsEXT(q, false));
	return RefAlpha(hit, material, t) >= hit.AlphaCutoff;
}

// How far along the ray the nearest surface is, among the instances `mask`
// lets in, or -1 where there is none.
float RefNearest(vec3 origin, vec3 direction, uint mask)
{
	rayQueryEXT q;
	rayQueryInitializeEXT(q, u_SceneAS, gl_RayFlagsNoneEXT, mask, origin, 0.0, direction, 1.0e6);
	while (rayQueryProceedEXT(q))
	{
		if (rayQueryGetIntersectionTypeEXT(q, false) == gl_RayQueryCandidateIntersectionTriangleEXT
			&& RefCandidateIsSurface(q))
			rayQueryConfirmIntersectionEXT(q);
	}
	return rayQueryGetIntersectionTypeEXT(q, true) == gl_RayQueryCommittedIntersectionNoneEXT
		 ? -1.0 : rayQueryGetIntersectionTEXT(q, true);
}

// --- texture footprints -----------------------------------------------------

// The level a map is read at: the cone's footprint in texels, its base (in
// uv units, log2) plus the map's own size.
float RefLod(uint slot, float base)
{
	const vec2 size = vec2(textureSize(u_Textures[nonuniformEXT(slot)], 0));
	return max(base + 0.5 * log2(max(size.x * size.y, 1.0)), 0.0);
}

vec4 RefMap(uint slot, vec2 uv, float base)
{
	return textureLod(u_Textures[nonuniformEXT(slot)], uv, RefLod(slot, base));
}

// log2 of the footprint's width in uv units for a uv mapping whose two edge
// steps are duv1 and duv2 over a triangle of world area `worldArea2` (both as
// parallelograms). Akenine-Moller et al. 2021: the cone's width over the
// cosine, times the square root of texels per square metre.
float RefFootprintBase(float footprint, vec2 duv1, vec2 duv2, float worldArea2)
{
	const float uvArea2 = abs(duv1.x * duv2.y - duv1.y * duv2.x);
	return log2(max(footprint, 1.0e-12)) + 0.5 * log2(max(uvArea2, 1.0e-24) / max(worldArea2, 1.0e-24));
}

// --- the surface at a hit ---------------------------------------------------

struct RefHit
{
	vec3  P;
	vec3  Ng;             // the triangle's, facing the ray
	vec3  N;              // the shading normal: smooth, then mapped
	vec3  T;              // the anisotropic lobe's tangent; zero for none
	vec3  Albedo;
	float Roughness;
	float Metallic;
	float Specular;
	vec3  Emissive;
	vec4  Coat;           // x clearcoat weight, y clearcoat roughness, z anisotropy, w wrap
	vec3  Sheen;
	float SheenRoughness;
	bool  Glass;
	float Opacity;        // glass: the share of the pane that is ordinary surface
	float PaneF0;         // glass: the clear share's reflectance, read as RefTransmittance reads it
	float Distance;       // from the ray's origin
	bool  Water;
	vec3  WaterSigma;     // water: Beer-Lambert's extinction per metre
	vec2  WaterWind;      // water: the wind's heading in world XZ, which the lobe stretches along
	vec3  WaterT;         // water: what the refracted ray's path lets through (set by the path)
	float WaterFoam;      // water: the foam's cover, which hides the bottom
	float WaterTime;      // water: the body's clock
	float WaterGradient;  // water: metres to deep water
	uint  WaterPattern;   // water: the foam pattern's slot, for the caustic web
	uint  Instance;       // the ray row hit
};

// One of a water vertex's two vec4 in the wave pass's surface buffer.
vec4 RefWaterVertex(RayFloats surface, uint vertex, uint which)
{
	const uint base = vertex * 8u + which * 4u;
	return vec4(surface.Floats[base + 0u], surface.Floats[base + 1u], surface.Floats[base + 2u],
				surface.Floats[base + 3u]);
}

// The foam pattern at a world coordinate scaled to `metres` a repeat, at the
// footprint's level for that scale.
float RefFoamPattern(uint slot, vec2 uv, float metres, float footprint)
{
	const float texels = float(textureSize(u_Textures[nonuniformEXT(slot)], 0).x);
	return textureLod(u_Textures[nonuniformEXT(slot)], uv,
					  max(log2(max(footprint / metres * texels, 1.0e-12)), 0.0)).r;
}

// The web of light a rippled surface focuses onto the bottom, as the frame's
// WaterCaustics (pbr_fragment.glsl) writes it, term for term: two reads of the
// lace drifting against each other, sharpened, and faded over the first stretch
// of depth. (A copy because the frame's reads its own bound sampler.)
float RefWaterCaustics(uint pattern, vec2 bottomXZ, float through, float gradientDepth, vec2 wind, float time)
{
	const float web1 = textureLod(u_Textures[nonuniformEXT(pattern)], bottomXZ / 2.9 + wind * (time * 0.050), 0.0).r;
	const float web2 = textureLod(u_Textures[nonuniformEXT(pattern)], bottomXZ / 1.9 - wind * (time * 0.037), 0.0).r;
	const float focus = clamp(1.0 - through / max(gradientDepth, 0.5), 0.0, 1.0);
	return web1 * web2 * 2.2 * focus * focus;
}

// The sea at a hit, as the water pass draws it: the wave normal its vertex
// stage interpolates, then the RV_WATER blocks of the lit shader's main (the
// detail ripples, the measured thickness and its colour, the wet crest, the
// footprint roughness), with foam left out. `footprint` is the cone's width
// over the slope, in metres.
void RefWaterSurface(inout RefHit h, RefWater W, RayInstance hit, RefTriangle t, mat4x3 worldToObject,
					 vec3 direction, float footprint)
{
	RayFloats surface = RayFloats(W.SurfaceAddress);
	const float w0 = 1.0 - t.Bary.x - t.Bary.y;
	const vec4 wave = RefWaterVertex(surface, t.I0, 0u) * w0 + RefWaterVertex(surface, t.I1, 0u) * t.Bary.x
					+ RefWaterVertex(surface, t.I2, 0u) * t.Bary.y;
	const float crest = RefWaterVertex(surface, t.I0, 1u).x * w0 + RefWaterVertex(surface, t.I1, 1u).x * t.Bary.x
					  + RefWaterVertex(surface, t.I2, 1u).x * t.Bary.y;
	vec3 N = normalize(vec3(dot(worldToObject[0], wave.xyz), dot(worldToObject[1], wave.xyz),
							dot(worldToObject[2], wave.xyz)));
	if (dot(N, h.Ng) < 0.0)
		N = -N;

	// The detail ripples: two reads of the tile, scrolled along the wind,
	// perturbing the normal in world XZ, faded with the camera's distance --
	// at the cone's level for each read's own metres per repeat.
	const float time = W.Deep.w;
	const vec2 wind = vec2(cos(W.Extra.x), sin(W.Extra.x));
	const float viewDistance = length(u_Ref.CameraPosition.xyz - h.P);
	const float texels = float(textureSize(u_Textures[nonuniformEXT(W.DetailSlot)], 0).x);
	const vec2 uv1 = h.P.xz / 6.1 + wind * (time * 0.110);
	const vec2 uv2 = h.P.xz / 2.3 - wind * (time * 0.067);
	const vec2 slope1 = textureLod(u_Textures[nonuniformEXT(W.DetailSlot)], uv1,
								   max(log2(max(footprint / 6.1 * texels, 1.0e-12)), 0.0)).xy * 2.0 - 1.0;
	const vec2 slope2 = textureLod(u_Textures[nonuniformEXT(W.DetailSlot)], uv2,
								   max(log2(max(footprint / 2.3 * texels, 1.0e-12)), 0.0)).xy * 2.0 - 1.0;
	const float detailFade = exp(-viewDistance * 0.010);
	N = normalize(N + vec3(slope1.x + slope2.x * 0.6, 0.0, slope1.y + slope2.y * 0.6) * (0.32 * detailFade));

	// The water behind the surface along the view, to the scene under it
	// (none in reach is deep water), and the colour it sets.
	const float behind = RefNearest(RefOffset(h.P, -h.Ng), direction, REF_MASK_DRY);
	const float thickness = (behind >= 0.0 ? behind : 1.0e6) * g_ViewDepthScale;
	const float gradient = max(W.Shallow.w, 0.05);

	// The foam, as the water pass builds it: the trails off the buffer at the
	// grid's rest position (fresh sheet barely cut by the lace, residual cut
	// into lace and wind-drawn streaks), the live crest where the surface
	// folds near the top of the swell, and the contact foam within a metre of
	// anything the water meets; the features sized by the body's wavelength,
	// and the whole scaled by its foam dial.
	RayFloats grid = RayFloats(hit.AttributeAddress);
	const uint gs = hit.AttributeStrideWords;
	const vec2 rest = vec2(grid.Floats[t.I0 * gs + 0u], grid.Floats[t.I0 * gs + 2u]) * w0
					+ vec2(grid.Floats[t.I1 * gs + 0u], grid.Floats[t.I1 * gs + 2u]) * t.Bary.x
					+ vec2(grid.Floats[t.I2 * gs + 0u], grid.Floats[t.I2 * gs + 2u]) * t.Bary.y;
	const vec2 trails = textureLod(u_Textures[nonuniformEXT(W.FoamSlot)],
								   rest / max(W.Size.xy, vec2(1.0e-3)) + 0.5, 0.0).rg;
	const float wavelength = max(W.Wave.y, 1.0);
	const vec2 windPerp = vec2(-wind.y, wind.x);
	const float lace1 = RefFoamPattern(W.PatternSlot, h.P.xz / (wavelength * 0.22) + wind * (time * 0.02),
									   wavelength * 0.22, footprint);
	const float lace2 = RefFoamPattern(W.PatternSlot, h.P.xz / (wavelength * 1.6), wavelength * 1.6, footprint);
	const float foamLace = clamp(lace1 * (0.35 + lace2 * 0.9), 0.0, 1.0);
	const float foamStreak = RefFoamPattern(W.PatternSlot, vec2(dot(h.P.xz, wind) / (wavelength * 1.6),
																dot(h.P.xz, windPerp) / (wavelength * 0.22)),
											wavelength * 0.22, footprint);
	const float foamNow = clamp((0.88 - wave.w) * 2.6, 0.0, 1.0) * smoothstep(0.55, 0.85, crest);
	float foam = clamp(max(trails.r * mix(foamLace, 1.0, 0.5) * 0.5 + trails.g * foamLace * foamStreak * 0.35,
						   foamNow * 0.22 * mix(foamLace, 1.0, 0.4)), 0.0, 1.0);
	const float shallow = 1.0 - smoothstep(0.1, 1.2, thickness);
	const float surge = 0.55 + 0.35 * sin(time * 1.1 + thickness * 3.0);
	const float contactLace = RefFoamPattern(W.PatternSlot, h.P.xz / (wavelength * 0.08) - wind * (time * 0.035),
											 wavelength * 0.08, footprint);
	foam = clamp(foam + shallow * surge * contactLace * 0.85, 0.0, 1.0);
	foam *= W.Extra.y;

	const float depthMix = 1.0 - exp(-thickness / gradient);
	vec3 albedo = mix(W.Shallow.rgb, W.Deep.rgb, depthMix);
	albedo = mix(albedo, W.Shallow.rgb, crest * 0.2);

	// The wet crest, smoother where no foam covers it; the foam white and
	// rough; then the roughness the camera's footprint grows toward the
	// Cox-Munk variance.
	const float wetness = smoothstep(1.0, 0.45, wave.w) * (1.0 - foam);
	float roughness = clamp(h.Roughness, 0.045, 1.0);
	roughness = clamp(roughness * mix(1.0, 0.45, wetness), 0.045, 1.0);
	albedo = mix(albedo, vec3(0.92, 0.95, 0.97), foam);
	roughness = clamp(mix(roughness, 0.72, foam), 0.045, 1.0);
	const float grazing = max(abs(dot(N, normalize(u_Ref.CameraPosition.xyz - h.P))), 0.08);
	const float pixelSea = viewDistance * 0.0016 / grazing;
	roughness = clamp(max(roughness, 0.24 * (1.0 - exp(-pixelSea * 0.045))), 0.045, 1.0);

	h.N = N;
	h.Albedo = albedo;
	h.Roughness = roughness;
	h.Metallic = 0.0;
	h.Emissive = vec3(0.0);
	h.Water = true;
	h.WaterSigma = vec3(4.6, 1.9, 1.3) / gradient;
	h.WaterWind = wind;
	h.WaterFoam = foam;
	h.WaterTime = time;
	h.WaterGradient = gradient;
	h.WaterPattern = W.PatternSlot;
}

// The four layers of a terrain chunk at a hit, as the layered lit shader's
// SampleSurface and SHADE_LAYER assemble them, at the cone's footprint where
// the frame takes the screen's. `Ns` is the smooth normal facing the ray, `V`
// the direction back along it.
void RefLayeredSurface(inout RefHit h, RefLayered L, vec3 Ns, vec3 V, vec2 uvM, vec2 duvM1, vec2 duvM2,
					   vec3 dp1, vec3 dp2, float worldArea2, float footprint)
{
	vec4 weight = textureLod(u_Textures[nonuniformEXT(L.WeightSlot.x)],
							 uvM * L.WeightUv.xy + L.WeightUv.zw, 0.0);
	for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i)
		if ((L.MapFlags[i] & REF_LAYER_ACTIVE) == 0)
			weight[i] = 0.0;
	const float sum = weight.x + weight.y + weight.z + weight.w;
	weight = sum > 1e-4 ? weight / sum : vec4(1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0);

	// The cliff projection: from the side the face turns towards, blended in as
	// the surface stands up. Metres per unit of uv from the edge that moves the
	// uv most, as the frame reads it off its derivatives.
	const float wall = 1.0 - smoothstep(0.50, 0.88, abs(Ns.y));
	const bool firstEdge = dot(duvM1, duvM1) >= dot(duvM2, duvM2);
	const vec2 duvE = firstEdge ? duvM1 : duvM2;
	const vec3 dpE = firstEdge ? dp1 : dp2;
	const float uvMetres = dot(duvE, duvE) > 1e-12 ? length(dpE.xz) / length(duvE) : 1.0;
	const float invMetres = 1.0 / max(uvMetres, 1e-4);
	const bool faceX = abs(Ns.x) > abs(Ns.z);
	const vec2 wallUv = (faceX ? vec2(h.P.z, -h.P.y) : vec2(h.P.x, -h.P.y)) * invMetres;
	const vec2 dWall1 = (faceX ? vec2(dp1.z, -dp1.y) : vec2(dp1.x, -dp1.y)) * invMetres;
	const vec2 dWall2 = (faceX ? vec2(dp2.z, -dp2.y) : vec2(dp2.x, -dp2.y)) * invMetres;

	vec4 base = vec4(0.0);
	float metallic = 0.0, roughness = 0.0, specular = 0.0;
	vec3 emissive = vec3(0.0), N = vec3(0.0);
	for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i)
	{
		const float w = weight[i];
		if (w <= 0.0)
			continue;
		const int flags = L.MapFlags[i];
		const vec4 tiling = L.UvTransform[i];
		vec2 uvL = uvM * tiling.xy + tiling.zw;
		vec2 uvW = wallUv * tiling.xy + tiling.zw;
		const vec2 duvL1 = duvM1 * tiling.xy, duvL2 = duvM2 * tiling.xy;
		const vec2 duvW1 = dWall1 * tiling.xy, duvW2 = dWall2 * tiling.xy;
		const float baseL = RefFootprintBase(footprint, duvL1, duvL2, worldArea2);
		const float baseW = RefFootprintBase(footprint, duvW1, duvW2, worldArea2);
		const mat3 TBN = TangentFrameOf(Ns, dp1, dp2, duvL1, duvL2);
		const mat3 TBNW = TangentFrameOf(Ns, dp1, dp2, duvW1, duvW2);
		const uint surfaceSlot = L.RoughnessSlots[i];

		const float pom = (flags & MAP_HEIGHT) != 0 ? L.HeightScale[i] * smoothstep(0.5, 0.8, w) : 0.0;
		if (pom > 0.0 && wall < 1.0)
			uvL = ParallaxLayer(surfaceSlot, uvL, normalize(transpose(TBN) * V),
								pom * (1.0 - wall), RefLod(surfaceSlot, baseL));
		if (pom > 0.0 && wall > 0.0)
			uvW = ParallaxLayer(surfaceSlot, uvW, normalize(transpose(TBNW) * V),
								pom * wall, RefLod(surfaceSlot, baseW));

		vec4 baseLayer = L.BaseColor[i];
		if ((flags & MAP_BASE_COLOR) != 0)
		{
			const vec4 floorT = RefMap(L.BaseColorSlots[i], uvL, baseL);
			baseLayer *= wall > 0.0 ? mix(floorT, RefMap(L.BaseColorSlots[i], uvW, baseW), wall) : floorT;
		}
		float roughLayer = L.Surface[i].y;
		if ((flags & MAP_ROUGHNESS) != 0)
		{
			const float floorR = RefMap(surfaceSlot, uvL, baseL).r;
			roughLayer *= wall > 0.0 ? mix(floorR, RefMap(surfaceSlot, uvW, baseW).r, wall) : floorR;
		}
		vec3 nLayer = Ns;
		if ((flags & MAP_NORMAL) != 0)
		{
			const vec3 nF = UnpackNormal(TBN, RefMap(L.NormalSlots[i], uvL, baseL).xy, L.Surface[i].w);
			const vec3 nW = UnpackNormal(TBNW, RefMap(L.NormalSlots[i], uvW, baseW).xy, L.Surface[i].w);
			nLayer = wall > 0.0 ? normalize(mix(nF, nW, wall)) : nF;
		}
		ApplyMacro(baseLayer.rgb, roughLayer, nLayer, Ns, h.P, L.MacroScale[i], L.MacroStrength[i]);
		base += w * baseLayer;
		metallic += w * L.Surface[i].x;
		roughness += w * roughLayer;
		specular += w * L.Specular[i];
		emissive += w * L.EmissiveColor[i].rgb;
		N += w * nLayer;
	}
	const float length2 = dot(N, N);
	h.N = length2 > 1e-8 ? N * inversesqrt(length2) : Ns;
	h.Albedo = base.rgb;
	h.Metallic = metallic;
	h.Roughness = roughness;
	h.Specular = specular;
	h.Emissive = emissive;
	// Off for terrain, as in the frame.
	h.T = vec3(0.0);
	h.Coat = vec4(0.0, 0.1, 0.0, 0.0);
	h.Sheen = vec3(0.0);
	h.SheenRoughness = 0.3;
}

// The nearest surface along the ray among the instances `mask` lets in, with
// its material read in full at the footprint of a cone `width` metres wide at
// the ray's origin.
bool RefTrace(vec3 origin, vec3 direction, float width, uint mask, out RefHit h)
{
	h.P = vec3(0.0); h.Ng = vec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0); h.N = h.Ng; h.T = vec3(0.0);
	h.Albedo = vec3(0.0); h.Roughness = 1.0; h.Metallic = 0.0; h.Specular = 0.5; h.Emissive = vec3(0.0);
	h.Coat = vec4(0.0, 0.1, 0.0, 0.0); h.Sheen = vec3(0.0); h.SheenRoughness = 0.3;
	h.Glass = false; h.Opacity = 1.0; h.PaneF0 = 0.04; h.Distance = 0.0;
	h.Water = false; h.WaterSigma = vec3(0.0); h.WaterWind = vec2(1.0, 0.0); h.WaterT = vec3(0.0);
	h.WaterFoam = 0.0; h.WaterTime = 0.0; h.WaterGradient = 1.0; h.WaterPattern = 0u;
	h.Instance = 0u;

	rayQueryEXT q;
	rayQueryInitializeEXT(q, u_SceneAS, gl_RayFlagsNoneEXT, mask, origin, 0.0, direction, 1.0e6);
	while (rayQueryProceedEXT(q))
	{
		if (rayQueryGetIntersectionTypeEXT(q, false) == gl_RayQueryCandidateIntersectionTriangleEXT
			&& RefCandidateIsSurface(q))
			rayQueryConfirmIntersectionEXT(q);
	}
	if (rayQueryGetIntersectionTypeEXT(q, true) == gl_RayQueryCommittedIntersectionNoneEXT)
		return false;

	const uint instance = uint(rayQueryGetIntersectionInstanceCustomIndexEXT(q, true));
	const mat4x3 objectToWorld = rayQueryGetIntersectionObjectToWorldEXT(q, true);
	const mat4x3 worldToObject = rayQueryGetIntersectionWorldToObjectEXT(q, true);
	const RayInstance hit = u_RayInstances.Instances[instance];
	const uint primitive = uint(rayQueryGetIntersectionPrimitiveIndexEXT(q, true));
	const RefTriangle t = RefTriangleOf(hit, primitive, rayQueryGetIntersectionBarycentricsEXT(q, true));
	h.Instance = instance;
	h.Distance = rayQueryGetIntersectionTEXT(q, true);
	const float w0 = 1.0 - t.Bary.x - t.Bary.y;
	RayFloats positions = RayFloats(hit.PositionAddress);
	RayFloats attributes = RayFloats(hit.AttributeAddress);
	const uint ps = hit.PositionStrideWords;
	const uint as_ = hit.AttributeStrideWords;

	// The point from the triangle itself, not origin + t * direction: the
	// next ray starts here, and the barycentric point lies on the surface.
	const vec3 p0 = vec3(positions.Floats[t.I0 * ps + 0u], positions.Floats[t.I0 * ps + 1u], positions.Floats[t.I0 * ps + 2u]);
	const vec3 p1 = vec3(positions.Floats[t.I1 * ps + 0u], positions.Floats[t.I1 * ps + 1u], positions.Floats[t.I1 * ps + 2u]);
	const vec3 p2 = vec3(positions.Floats[t.I2 * ps + 0u], positions.Floats[t.I2 * ps + 1u], positions.Floats[t.I2 * ps + 2u]);
	h.P = objectToWorld * vec4(p0 * w0 + p1 * t.Bary.x + p2 * t.Bary.y, 1.0);

	// The edges in the world: the face normal (exact under any scale), the
	// triangle's area for the texel density, and the two steps the tangent
	// frame is built from.
	const vec3 dp1 = objectToWorld * vec4(p1 - p0, 0.0);
	const vec3 dp2 = objectToWorld * vec4(p2 - p0, 0.0);
	const vec3 face = cross(dp1, dp2);
	const float worldArea2 = length(face);
	h.Ng = worldArea2 > 0.0 ? face / worldArea2 : vec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0);

	vec3 objectN = cross(p1 - p0, p2 - p0);
	if ((hit.Flags & RAY_INSTANCE_POSED) == 0u)
	{
		const vec3 n0 = vec3(attributes.Floats[t.I0 * as_ + 3u], attributes.Floats[t.I0 * as_ + 4u], attributes.Floats[t.I0 * as_ + 5u]);
		const vec3 n1 = vec3(attributes.Floats[t.I1 * as_ + 3u], attributes.Floats[t.I1 * as_ + 4u], attributes.Floats[t.I1 * as_ + 5u]);
		const vec3 n2 = vec3(attributes.Floats[t.I2 * as_ + 3u], attributes.Floats[t.I2 * as_ + 4u], attributes.Floats[t.I2 * as_ + 5u]);
		objectN = n0 * w0 + n1 * t.Bary.x + n2 * t.Bary.y;
	}
	vec3 Ns = normalize(vec3(dot(worldToObject[0], objectN), dot(worldToObject[1], objectN),
							 dot(worldToObject[2], objectN)));

	// Two-sided, as the frame draws it: both normals turned to face the ray.
	if (dot(h.Ng, direction) > 0.0)
		h.Ng = -h.Ng;
	if (dot(Ns, h.Ng) < 0.0)
		Ns = -Ns;

	const vec3 V = -direction;
	const vec2 uv0 = RefCornerUv(hit, t.I0), uv1 = RefCornerUv(hit, t.I1), uv2 = RefCornerUv(hit, t.I2);
	const vec2 uvM = uv0 * w0 + uv1 * t.Bary.x + uv2 * t.Bary.y;
	const vec2 duvM1 = uv1 - uv0, duvM2 = uv2 - uv0;
	const float footprint = (width + g_ConeSpread * h.Distance) / max(abs(dot(h.Ng, direction)), 1.0e-4);
	const GpuMaterial material = u_Materials.Materials[hit.MaterialIndex];

	if ((hit.Flags & RAY_INSTANCE_WATER) != 0u)
	{
		h.Roughness = hit.Surface.y;
		h.Specular = material.Specular;
		RefWaterSurface(h, u_RefWater.Records[u_RefRowExtra.Rows[instance]], hit, t, worldToObject, direction,
						footprint);
	}
	else if ((hit.Flags & RAY_INSTANCE_LAYERED) != 0u)
	{
		RefLayeredSurface(h, u_RefLayered.Records[u_RefRowExtra.Rows[instance]], Ns, V, uvM, duvM1, duvM2,
						  dp1, dp2, worldArea2, footprint);
	}
	else
	{
		// SampleSurface's single-material body, at the cone's footprint.
		vec2 uv = uvM * material.UvTransform.xy + material.UvTransform.zw;
		const vec2 duv1 = duvM1 * material.UvTransform.xy, duv2 = duvM2 * material.UvTransform.xy;
		const float base = RefFootprintBase(footprint, duv1, duv2, worldArea2);
		const mat3 TBN = TangentFrameOf(Ns, dp1, dp2, duv1, duv2);
		if ((material.MapFlags & MAP_HEIGHT) != 0)
			uv = ParallaxMarch(material.Maps1.w, uv, transpose(TBN) * V,
							   material.HeightScale, RefLod(material.Maps1.w, base));

		h.Albedo = hit.BaseColor.rgb;
		if ((material.MapFlags & MAP_BASE_COLOR) != 0)
			h.Albedo *= RefMap(material.Maps0.x, uv, base).rgb;
		h.Roughness = hit.Surface.y;
		if ((material.MapFlags & MAP_ROUGHNESS) != 0)
			h.Roughness *= RefMap(material.Maps1.x, uv, base).r;
		h.Metallic = hit.Surface.x;
		if ((material.MapFlags & MAP_METALLIC) != 0)
			h.Metallic *= RefMap(material.Maps1.y, uv, base).r;
		h.N = Ns;
		if ((material.MapFlags & MAP_NORMAL) != 0)
			h.N = UnpackNormal(TBN, RefMap(material.Maps0.y, uv, base).xy, hit.Surface.w);
		h.Specular = material.Specular;
		if ((material.MapFlags & MAP_SPECULAR) != 0)
			h.Specular *= RefMap(material.Maps1.z, uv, base).r;
		h.Emissive = RefEmission(instance, primitive, t.Bary);
		ApplyMacro(h.Albedo, h.Roughness, h.N, Ns, h.P, material.Macro.x, material.Macro.y);
		h.T = TBN[0];
		h.Coat = vec4(material.Clearcoat, material.ClearcoatRoughness, material.Anisotropy, material.Subsurface);
		h.Sheen = material.SheenColor;
		h.SheenRoughness = material.SheenRoughness;
	}

	h.Glass = (hit.Flags & RAY_INSTANCE_TRANSMISSIVE) != 0u;
	if (h.Glass)
	{
		h.Opacity = clamp(RefAlpha(hit, material, t), 0.0, 1.0);
		h.PaneF0 = RefPaneF0(hit, material, t);
	}

	h.Albedo = clamp(h.Albedo, 0.0, 1.0);
	h.Metallic = clamp(h.Metallic, 0.0, 1.0);
	h.Specular = clamp(h.Specular, 0.0, 1.0);
	h.Roughness = clamp(h.Roughness, REF_ROUGHNESS_FLOOR, 1.0);
	return true;
}

// What reaches `reach` along the ray: zero past anything solid, and through
// glass the product of each pane's clear share times what its Fresnel lets
// through at that angle. A crossing reported twice (the hardware may) is
// counted once: up to eight remembered, more than any light here crosses.
vec3 RefTransmittance(vec3 origin, vec3 direction, float reach)
{
	vec3 through = vec3(1.0);
	uvec2 seen[8];
	int seenCount = 0;
	rayQueryEXT q;
	rayQueryInitializeEXT(q, u_SceneAS, gl_RayFlagsTerminateOnFirstHitEXT, REF_MASK_DRY,
						  origin, 0.0, direction, reach);
	while (rayQueryProceedEXT(q))
	{
		if (rayQueryGetIntersectionTypeEXT(q, false) != gl_RayQueryCandidateIntersectionTriangleEXT)
			continue;
		const uint instance = uint(rayQueryGetIntersectionInstanceCustomIndexEXT(q, false));
		RayInstance hit = u_RayInstances.Instances[instance];
		if ((hit.Flags & RAY_INSTANCE_TRANSMISSIVE) == 0u)
		{
			if (RefCandidateIsSurface(q))
				rayQueryConfirmIntersectionEXT(q);
			continue;
		}
		const uint primitive = uint(rayQueryGetIntersectionPrimitiveIndexEXT(q, false));
		bool counted = false;
		for (int i = 0; i < seenCount; ++i)
			counted = counted || (seen[i].x == instance && seen[i].y == primitive);
		if (counted)
			continue;
		if (seenCount < 8)
			seen[seenCount++] = uvec2(instance, primitive);

		const GpuMaterial material = u_Materials.Materials[hit.MaterialIndex];
		const RefTriangle t = RefTriangleOf(hit, primitive, rayQueryGetIntersectionBarycentricsEXT(q, false));
		RayFloats positions = RayFloats(hit.PositionAddress);
		const uint ps = hit.PositionStrideWords;
		const vec3 p0 = vec3(positions.Floats[t.I0 * ps + 0u], positions.Floats[t.I0 * ps + 1u], positions.Floats[t.I0 * ps + 2u]);
		const vec3 p1 = vec3(positions.Floats[t.I1 * ps + 0u], positions.Floats[t.I1 * ps + 1u], positions.Floats[t.I1 * ps + 2u]);
		const vec3 p2 = vec3(positions.Floats[t.I2 * ps + 0u], positions.Floats[t.I2 * ps + 1u], positions.Floats[t.I2 * ps + 2u]);
		const mat4x3 objectToWorld = rayQueryGetIntersectionObjectToWorldEXT(q, false);
		const vec3 Ng = normalize(cross(objectToWorld * vec4(p1 - p0, 0.0), objectToWorld * vec4(p2 - p0, 0.0)));
		const float F = FresnelSchlick(abs(dot(Ng, direction)), vec3(RefPaneF0(hit, material, t))).x;
		through *= (1.0 - clamp(RefAlpha(hit, material, t), 0.0, 1.0)) * (1.0 - F);
		if (max(through.r, max(through.g, through.b)) <= 0.0)
		{
			rayQueryTerminateEXT(q);
			return vec3(0.0);
		}
	}
	if (rayQueryGetIntersectionTypeEXT(q, true) != gl_RayQueryCommittedIntersectionNoneEXT)
		return vec3(0.0);
	return through;
}

vec3 RefSky(vec3 direction)
{
	return textureLod(u_Environment, vec4(RotateIntoSky(direction), 0.0), 0.0).rgb * u_Scene.Environment.x;
}

// --- the material: the lit shader's model, exactly --------------------------

float RefLuminance(vec3 c)
{
	return dot(c, vec3(0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722));
}

vec3 RefF0(RefHit h)
{
	return mix(vec3(0.08 * h.Specular), h.Albedo, h.Metallic);
}

mat3 RefBasis(vec3 n)
{
	const vec3 up = abs(n.z) < 0.999 ? vec3(0.0, 0.0, 1.0) : vec3(1.0, 0.0, 0.0);
	const vec3 t = normalize(cross(up, n));
	return mat3(t, cross(n, t), n);
}

// The base lobe's frame and its two widths in GGX's alpha: anisotropic about
// the tangent where the material asks for it and has one (the frame's
// condition and its Disney remap), otherwise any frame about N and one alpha.
// True when anisotropic.
bool RefBaseLobe(RefHit h, out mat3 frame, out float ax, out float ay)
{
	const float alpha = h.Roughness * h.Roughness;
	if (abs(h.Coat.z) > 0.001 && dot(h.T, h.T) > 0.0)
	{
		const vec3 T = normalize(h.T - h.N * dot(h.T, h.N));
		frame = mat3(T, cross(h.N, T), h.N);
		const float aspect = sqrt(1.0 - abs(h.Coat.z) * 0.9);
		ax = max(alpha / aspect, 0.001);
		ay = max(alpha * aspect, 0.001);
		if (h.Coat.z < 0.0)
		{
			const float swap = ax;
			ax = ay;
			ay = swap;
		}
		return true;
	}
	frame = RefBasis(h.N);
	ax = alpha;
	ay = alpha;
	return false;
}

// Smith's Lambda for the lobe's widths, toward a direction above its frame:
// exact for GGX, anisotropic where ax and ay differ.
float RefSmithLambda(vec3 w, float ax, float ay)
{
	return 0.5 * (-1.0 + sqrt(1.0 + (ax * ax * w.x * w.x + ay * ay * w.y * w.y) / (w.z * w.z)));
}

// The base lobe's specular for a given F0: NDF x G x F over (4 N.V N.L), with
// the frame's distribution and Fresnel and the exact height-correlated Smith
// term (the header says why). Without the cosine. Returns F too, for the
// diffuse's share.
vec3 RefBaseSpecular(RefHit h, vec3 V, vec3 L, vec3 F0, out vec3 F)
{
	const vec3 H = normalize(V + L);
	mat3 frame;
	float ax, ay;
	RefBaseLobe(h, frame, ax, ay);
	const float NDF = DistributionGGXAniso(max(dot(h.N, H), 0.0), dot(frame[0], H), dot(frame[1], H), ax, ay);
	F = FresnelSchlick(max(dot(H, V), 0.0), F0);
	const vec3 Vl = transpose(frame) * V;
	const vec3 Ll = transpose(frame) * L;
	if (Vl.z <= 0.0 || Ll.z <= 0.0)
		return vec3(0.0);
	const float G = 1.0 / (1.0 + RefSmithLambda(Vl, ax, ay) + RefSmithLambda(Ll, ax, ay));
	return NDF * G * F / (4.0 * Vl.z * Ll.z);
}

// The ordinary surface, f x cosine: what one unit of radiance arriving along
// L sends back along V. The frame's light loop term by term -- base specular,
// the clearcoat's share taken first, the sheen on top, the diffuse wrapped
// where asked -- for a light it does not skip (N.L above zero). Zero below the
// triangle too: light does not come through a surface, whatever the mapped
// normal says.
vec3 RefSurfaceCos(RefHit h, vec3 V, vec3 L)
{
	const float NdotL = max(dot(h.N, L), 0.0);
	if (NdotL <= 0.0 || dot(h.Ng, L) <= 0.0)
		return vec3(0.0);
	const float NdotVc = max(dot(h.N, V), 0.0);
	vec3 F;
	vec3 specular = RefBaseSpecular(h, V, L, RefF0(h), F);
	vec3 kD = (vec3(1.0) - F) * (1.0 - h.Metallic);
	const vec3 H = normalize(V + L);
	if (h.Coat.x > 0.0)
	{
		const float VdotH = max(dot(V, H), 0.0);
		const float coatRoughness = clamp(h.Coat.y, 0.045, 1.0);
		const mat3 coatFrame = RefBasis(h.N);
		const float coatAlpha = coatRoughness * coatRoughness;
		const float Dc = DistributionGGXAniso(max(dot(h.N, H), 0.0), dot(coatFrame[0], H), dot(coatFrame[1], H),
											  coatAlpha, coatAlpha);
		const float Vc = VisibilityKelemen(VdotH);
		const float Fc = (0.04 + 0.96 * Pow5(1.0 - VdotH)) * h.Coat.x;
		specular = specular * (1.0 - Fc) + vec3(Dc * Vc * Fc);
		kD *= (1.0 - Fc);
	}
	if (dot(h.Sheen, h.Sheen) > 0.0)
	{
		const float Ds = DistributionCharlie(max(dot(h.N, H), 0.0), clamp(h.SheenRoughness, 0.07, 1.0));
		const float Vs = VisibilityAshikhmin(NdotVc, NdotL);
		specular += h.Sheen * Ds * Vs;
	}
	const float diffuseCosine = h.Coat.w > 0.0 ? WrapDiffuse(dot(h.N, L), h.Coat.w) : NdotL;
	return kD * h.Albedo / PI * diffuseCosine + specular * NdotL;
}

// A pane's clear share, f x cosine: the dielectric's reflection through the
// pane's own lobe (its straight-through share is a delta no light sample can
// land on; the path continues through it instead).
vec3 RefClearCos(RefHit h, vec3 V, vec3 L)
{
	const float NdotL = max(dot(h.N, L), 0.0);
	if (NdotL <= 0.0 || dot(h.Ng, L) <= 0.0)
		return vec3(0.0);
	vec3 F;
	return RefBaseSpecular(h, V, L, vec3(h.PaneF0), F) * NdotL;
}

// The water's lobe frame: Beckmann, anisotropic about the wind flattened onto
// the surface, at the widths the frame's water branch gives it.
void RefWaterLobe(RefHit h, out vec3 T, out vec3 B, out float ax, out float ay)
{
	const vec3 wind = vec3(h.WaterWind.x, 0.0, h.WaterWind.y);
	T = normalize(wind - h.N * dot(wind, h.N));
	B = cross(h.N, T);
	ax = max(h.Roughness * 1.16, 0.02);
	ay = max(h.Roughness * 0.86, 0.02);
}

// What the water's surface reflects, f x cosine: the frame's Beckmann
// distribution and Fresnel, with its Smith G1 made height-correlated
// (Lambda = 1 / G1 - 1, the owner's exact masking for every lobe).
vec3 RefWaterSpecularCos(RefHit h, vec3 V, vec3 L)
{
	const float NdotL = dot(h.N, L);
	const float NdotV = dot(h.N, V);
	if (NdotL <= 0.0 || NdotV <= 0.0 || dot(h.Ng, L) <= 0.0)
		return vec3(0.0);
	vec3 T, B;
	float ax, ay;
	RefWaterLobe(h, T, B, ax, ay);
	const vec3 H = normalize(V + L);
	const float D = WaterBeckmannDX(H, h.N, T, B, ax, ay);
	const float g1v = WaterBeckmannG1X(V, h.N, T, B, ax, ay);
	const float g1l = WaterBeckmannG1X(L, h.N, T, B, ax, ay);
	if (D <= 0.0 || g1v <= 0.0 || g1l <= 0.0)
		return vec3(0.0);
	const float G = 1.0 / (1.0 / g1v + 1.0 / g1l - 1.0);
	const vec3 F = FresnelSchlick(max(dot(H, V), 0.0), RefF0(h));
	return D * G * F / (4.0 * NdotV);
}

// The water's lit body, f x cosine: its colour as a diffuse term with the
// light loop's (1 - F), and only the share the refracted path does not let
// through -- the frame's `scatter * (1 - T)`.
vec3 RefWaterScatterCos(RefHit h, vec3 V, vec3 L)
{
	const float NdotL = dot(h.N, L);
	if (NdotL <= 0.0 || dot(h.Ng, L) <= 0.0)
		return vec3(0.0);
	const vec3 F = FresnelSchlick(max(dot(normalize(V + L), V), 0.0), RefF0(h));
	return (vec3(1.0) - h.WaterT) * (vec3(1.0) - F) * h.Albedo / PI * NdotL;
}

// A direction from the water's Beckmann lobe: a facet normal drawn in
// proportion to D(H) cos (Walter et al. 2007, anisotropic), reflected.
vec3 RefSampleWater(RefHit h, vec3 V)
{
	vec3 T, B;
	float ax, ay;
	RefWaterLobe(h, T, B, ax, ay);
	const float u1 = RefRandom();
	const float u2 = RefRandom();
	const float phi = atan(ay * sin(2.0 * PI * u1), ax * cos(2.0 * PI * u1));
	const float c = cos(phi);
	const float s = sin(phi);
	const float tan2 = -log(max(1.0 - u2, 1.0e-12)) / (c * c / (ax * ax) + s * s / (ay * ay));
	const float cosTheta = inversesqrt(1.0 + tan2);
	const float sinTheta = sqrt(max(0.0, 1.0 - cosTheta * cosTheta));
	const vec3 H = normalize(T * (sinTheta * c) + B * (sinTheta * s) + h.N * cosTheta);
	return reflect(-V, H);
}

float RefWaterPdf(RefHit h, vec3 V, vec3 L)
{
	vec3 T, B;
	float ax, ay;
	RefWaterLobe(h, T, B, ax, ay);
	const vec3 H = normalize(V + L);
	const float VdotH = dot(V, H);
	if (VdotH <= 0.0)
		return 0.0;
	return WaterBeckmannDX(H, h.N, T, B, ax, ay) * max(dot(h.N, H), 0.0) / (4.0 * VdotH);
}

// Everything a light can reach at this vertex, f x cosine.
vec3 RefBsdfCos(RefHit h, vec3 V, vec3 L)
{
	if (h.Water)
		return RefWaterSpecularCos(h, V, L) + RefWaterScatterCos(h, V, L);
	if (!h.Glass)
		return RefSurfaceCos(h, V, L);
	return h.Opacity * RefSurfaceCos(h, V, L) + (1.0 - h.Opacity) * RefClearCos(h, V, L);
}

// --- sampling the material --------------------------------------------------
//
// Three samplers, chosen by a mixture and weighed by its whole density, so the
// estimate is f cos over the mixture's pdf whichever drew the direction: the
// base lobe by GGX's visible normals (anisotropic where the lobe is), the coat
// the same at its own roughness, and the diffuse from its own wrapped cosine,
// which also covers the sheen. The diffuse sampler covers the whole upper
// hemisphere and is never chosen less than one time in twenty, so every
// direction the material reflects into has a density.

// GGX's visible normals (Heitz 2018) for widths ax, ay, in the frame where the
// lobe's tangent is +x and N is +z.
vec3 RefSampleVisibleNormal(vec3 Ve, float ax, float ay, vec2 u)
{
	const vec3 Vh = normalize(vec3(ax * Ve.x, ay * Ve.y, Ve.z));
	const float lensq = Vh.x * Vh.x + Vh.y * Vh.y;
	const vec3 T1 = lensq > 0.0 ? vec3(-Vh.y, Vh.x, 0.0) * inversesqrt(lensq) : vec3(1.0, 0.0, 0.0);
	const vec3 T2 = cross(Vh, T1);
	const float r = sqrt(u.x);
	const float phi = 2.0 * PI * u.y;
	const float t1 = r * cos(phi);
	float t2 = r * sin(phi);
	const float s = 0.5 * (1.0 + Vh.z);
	t2 = (1.0 - s) * sqrt(1.0 - t1 * t1) + s * t2;
	const vec3 Nh = t1 * T1 + t2 * T2 + sqrt(max(0.0, 1.0 - t1 * t1 - t2 * t2)) * Vh;
	return normalize(vec3(ax * Nh.x, ay * Nh.y, max(0.0, Nh.z)));
}

vec3 RefSampleLobe(mat3 frame, float ax, float ay, vec3 V)
{
	const vec3 Hl = RefSampleVisibleNormal(transpose(frame) * V, ax, ay, vec2(RefRandom(), RefRandom()));
	return reflect(-V, frame * Hl);
}

// The density of a direction drawn by RefSampleLobe: D(H) G1(V) / (4 N.V),
// with the exact anisotropic Smith G1 the visible-normal sampler implies.
float RefLobePdf(mat3 frame, float ax, float ay, vec3 V, vec3 L)
{
	const vec3 Vl = transpose(frame) * V;
	if (Vl.z <= 0.0)
		return 0.0;
	const vec3 Hl = transpose(frame) * normalize(V + L);
	if (Hl.z <= 0.0)
		return 0.0;
	const float D = DistributionGGXAniso(Hl.z, Hl.x, Hl.y, ax, ay);
	return D / (1.0 + RefSmithLambda(Vl, ax, ay)) / (4.0 * Vl.z);
}

// The wrapped diffuse's own distribution over the upper hemisphere: density
// in proportion to (N.L + wrap), which is the cosine when wrap is zero.
vec3 RefSampleDiffuse(RefHit h)
{
	const float w = max(h.Coat.w, 0.0);
	const float mu = -w + sqrt(w * w + RefRandom() * (1.0 + 2.0 * w));
	const float phi = 2.0 * PI * RefRandom();
	const float sine = sqrt(max(0.0, 1.0 - mu * mu));
	return RefBasis(h.N) * vec3(sine * cos(phi), sine * sin(phi), mu);
}

float RefDiffusePdf(RefHit h, vec3 L)
{
	const float mu = dot(h.N, L);
	const float w = max(h.Coat.w, 0.0);
	return mu > 0.0 ? (mu + w) / (PI * (1.0 + 2.0 * w)) : 0.0;
}

// How often each sampler is chosen: base, coat, diffuse, from each one's share
// of what the surface reflects at this view.
vec3 RefChances(RefHit h, vec3 V)
{
	const float NdotV = dot(h.N, V);
	if (NdotV <= 0.0)
		return vec3(0.0, 0.0, 1.0);
	const vec3 F = FresnelSchlick(NdotV, RefF0(h));
	const float Fc = h.Coat.x > 0.0 ? (0.04 + 0.96 * Pow5(1.0 - NdotV)) * h.Coat.x : 0.0;
	const float base = RefLuminance(F) * (1.0 - Fc);
	const float diffuse = RefLuminance((vec3(1.0) - F) * (1.0 - h.Metallic) * h.Albedo) * (1.0 - Fc)
						+ RefLuminance(h.Sheen);
	const float total = base + Fc + diffuse;
	if (total <= 0.0)
		return vec3(0.0, 0.0, 1.0);
	const float d = max(diffuse / total, 0.05);
	const float rest = base + Fc;
	return rest > 0.0 ? vec3(base / rest * (1.0 - d), Fc / rest * (1.0 - d), d) : vec3(0.0, 0.0, 1.0);
}

// The density of the ordinary surface's mixture for a direction: what
// RefSampleSurfaceDirection draws from.
float RefSurfacePdf(RefHit h, vec3 V, vec3 L)
{
	mat3 frame;
	float ax, ay;
	RefBaseLobe(h, frame, ax, ay);
	const mat3 coatFrame = RefBasis(h.N);
	const float coatRoughness = clamp(h.Coat.y, 0.045, 1.0);
	const float coatAlpha = coatRoughness * coatRoughness;
	const vec3 chance = RefChances(h, V);
	float pdf = chance.z * RefDiffusePdf(h, L);
	if (chance.x > 0.0)
		pdf += chance.x * RefLobePdf(frame, ax, ay, V, L);
	if (chance.y > 0.0)
		pdf += chance.y * RefLobePdf(coatFrame, coatAlpha, coatAlpha, V, L);
	return pdf;
}

// A direction from the ordinary surface's mixture of samplers.
vec3 RefSampleSurfaceDirection(RefHit h, vec3 V)
{
	const vec3 chance = RefChances(h, V);
	const float pick = RefRandom();
	if (pick < chance.x)
	{
		mat3 frame;
		float ax, ay;
		RefBaseLobe(h, frame, ax, ay);
		return RefSampleLobe(frame, ax, ay, V);
	}
	if (pick < chance.x + chance.y)
	{
		const float coatRoughness = clamp(h.Coat.y, 0.045, 1.0);
		const float coatAlpha = coatRoughness * coatRoughness;
		return RefSampleLobe(RefBasis(h.N), coatAlpha, coatAlpha, V);
	}
	return RefSampleDiffuse(h);
}

// Water's choices: how often the surface reflects (by its Fresnel at this
// view), and how often what enters reaches the bottom (by what it lets through).
void RefWaterChances(RefHit h, vec3 V, out float Fv, out float pReflect, out float pBottom)
{
	Fv = FresnelSchlick(max(dot(h.N, V), 0.0), RefF0(h)).x;
	pReflect = clamp(Fv, 0.05, 0.95);
	pBottom = max(h.WaterT.r, max(h.WaterT.g, h.WaterT.b)) > 0.0 ? clamp(RefLuminance(h.WaterT), 0.05, 0.95) : 0.0;
}

// A pane's clear share reflects by its Fresnel against the triangle -- what
// RefTransmittance lets through for a light behind it is the rest.
float RefPaneReflectChance(RefHit h, vec3 V)
{
	return FresnelSchlick(abs(dot(h.Ng, V)), vec3(h.PaneF0)).x;
}

// The density with which the path's choice at this vertex lands on a
// direction, over every choice that is not a delta (glass's straight-through,
// water's refraction): what the weighting between a light sample and the path
// (MIS) needs on the path's side.
float RefBsdfPdf(RefHit h, vec3 V, vec3 L)
{
	if (h.Water)
	{
		float Fv, pReflect, pBottom;
		RefWaterChances(h, V, Fv, pReflect, pBottom);
		return pReflect * RefWaterPdf(h, V, L) + (1.0 - pReflect) * (1.0 - pBottom) * RefDiffusePdf(h, L);
	}
	const float surface = RefSurfacePdf(h, V, L);
	if (!h.Glass)
		return surface;
	mat3 frame;
	float ax, ay;
	RefBaseLobe(h, frame, ax, ay);
	return h.Opacity * surface + (1.0 - h.Opacity) * RefPaneReflectChance(h, V) * RefLobePdf(frame, ax, ay, V, L);
}

// Veach's power heuristic: the weight of the strategy with density `a`
// against the one with density `b`.
float RefPowerHeuristic(float a, float b)
{
	const float a2 = a * a;
	return a2 / max(a2 + b * b, 1.0e-30);
}

// --- lamps: the lit shader's lights, with their real shapes -----------------
//
// The frame lights a lamp as a point of intensity I (colour times intensity)
// with a range window and a spot's ramp; its size (SourceRadius, and with
// SourceLength along its axis a capsule) changes, in the frame's own words,
// only the image it makes in shiny surfaces. So the reference gives the shape
// the same total light as the frame's point -- a uniform radiance of 4 I / A
// over its area A = 2 pi r l + 4 pi r^2, which for a sphere is I / (pi r^2) and
// from far off is the point again -- and keeps the window and the ramp the
// lamp's own, taken from its centre as the frame takes them. A lamp of no
// radius stays a point (only a light sample finds it), and so does a
// directional light. The shapes are not geometry: they hide nothing, and the
// camera does not see them, as the frame's camera does not; a path that has
// scattered meets them, and is weighed against the light samples (MIS).
//
// Which lamp a vertex samples: each in proportion to its light there as a
// point (through its window and ramp, inverse square to its centre, never
// nearer than its own size), so the lamps out of range of a bridge pixel cost
// it nothing.

// The window and the ramp at P, from the lamp's centre; one for a sun.
float RefLampScale(GpuLight light, vec3 P)
{
	if (light.Position.w == 0.0)
		return 1.0;
	const vec3 toLight = light.Position.xyz - P;
	const float distance2 = dot(toLight, toLight);
	const float range = max(light.Params.x, 0.0001);
	const float t = distance2 / (range * range);
	const float ratio = clamp(1.0 - t * t, 0.0, 1.0);
	float scale = ratio * ratio;
	const float cosInner = light.Params.y;
	const float cosOuter = light.Params.z;
	if (cosOuter < cosInner && distance2 > 0.0)
		scale *= clamp((dot(toLight * inversesqrt(distance2), -light.Direction.xyz) - cosOuter)
					   / max(cosInner - cosOuter, 0.0001), 0.0, 1.0);
	return scale;
}

bool RefLampShaped(GpuLight light)
{
	return light.Position.w != 0.0 && light.Direction.w > 0.0;
}

float RefLampLength(GpuLight light)
{
	return max(light.Extent.x, 0.0);
}

float RefLampWeight(GpuLight light, vec3 P)
{
	const float power = RefLuminance(light.Color.rgb * light.Color.a);
	if (light.Position.w == 0.0)
		return power;
	const vec3 toLight = light.Position.xyz - P;
	const float size = max(light.Direction.w, 0.0) + 0.5 * RefLampLength(light);
	return power * RefLampScale(light, P) / max(dot(toLight, toLight), max(size * size, 1.0e-4));
}

float RefLampTotal(vec3 P)
{
	float total = 0.0;
	for (int i = 0; i < u_Scene.LightCount; ++i)
		total += RefLampWeight(u_Lights.Lights[i], P);
	return total;
}

// What a shaped lamp's surface emits toward a vertex at P.
vec3 RefLampRadiance(GpuLight light, vec3 P)
{
	const float r = light.Direction.w;
	const float area = 2.0 * PI * r * RefLampLength(light) + 4.0 * PI * r * r;
	return light.Color.rgb * light.Color.a * RefLampScale(light, P) * (4.0 / area);
}

// A sphere's directions from P: the cone it subtends, sampled uniformly. The
// cone's size as 1 - cos without the cancellation, for lamps a kilometre off.
float RefSphereCone(vec3 C, float R, vec3 P)
{
	const vec3 toC = C - P;
	const float d2 = dot(toC, toC);
	if (d2 <= R * R)
		return 0.0;
	const float sin2 = R * R / d2;
	return sin2 / (1.0 + sqrt(max(0.0, 1.0 - sin2)));
}

bool RefSampleSphere(vec3 C, float R, vec3 P, out vec3 L, out float dist, out float pdf)
{
	const float cone = RefSphereCone(C, R, P);
	if (cone <= 0.0)
		return false;
	const vec3 toC = C - P;
	const float d2 = dot(toC, toC);
	const float om = RefRandom() * cone;
	const float cosT = 1.0 - om;
	const float sinT = sqrt(max(0.0, om * (2.0 - om)));
	const float phi = 2.0 * PI * RefRandom();
	L = RefBasis(toC * inversesqrt(d2)) * vec3(sinT * cos(phi), sinT * sin(phi), cosT);
	const float b = dot(toC, L);
	dist = b - sqrt(max(b * b - (d2 - R * R), 0.0));
	pdf = 1.0 / (2.0 * PI * cone);
	return dist > 0.0;
}

// A capsule as seen from P: its centre, axis, half length and radius; the
// directions across its side toward P (U) and around it (W); the half angle of
// the side P can see; and how often the side is chosen over the end caps.
struct RefCapsule
{
	vec3  C;
	vec3  A;
	float H;
	float R;
	vec3  U;
	vec3  W;
	float Alpha;
	float PSide;
};

RefCapsule RefCapsuleFrom(GpuLight light, vec3 P)
{
	RefCapsule c;
	c.C = light.Position.xyz;
	c.A = normalize(light.Extent.yzw);
	c.H = 0.5 * RefLampLength(light);
	c.R = light.Direction.w;
	const vec3 v = P - c.C;
	const vec3 q = v - c.A * dot(v, c.A);
	const float rho = length(q);
	c.U = rho > 1.0e-6 ? q / rho : RefBasis(c.A)[0];
	c.W = cross(c.A, c.U);
	c.Alpha = rho > c.R ? acos(clamp(c.R / rho, 0.0, 1.0)) : 0.0;
	const float side = 2.0 * c.H * c.R * 2.0 * c.Alpha;
	c.PSide = side / (side + PI * c.R * c.R);
	return c;
}

// The density of a point on the capsule, per unit area: on the side, uniform
// over the part P can see; on an end, uniform over that end's whole sphere
// (the half inside the side is drawn and refused).
float RefCapsuleAreaPdf(RefCapsule c, vec3 x)
{
	if (abs(dot(x - c.C, c.A)) <= c.H)
		return c.Alpha > 0.0 ? c.PSide / (2.0 * c.H * c.R * 2.0 * c.Alpha) : 0.0;
	return (1.0 - c.PSide) * 0.5 / (4.0 * PI * c.R * c.R);
}

bool RefSampleCapsule(RefCapsule c, vec3 P, out vec3 x, out vec3 n)
{
	if (RefRandom() < c.PSide)
	{
		const float s = (2.0 * RefRandom() - 1.0) * c.H;
		const float phi = (2.0 * RefRandom() - 1.0) * c.Alpha;
		n = c.U * cos(phi) + c.W * sin(phi);
		x = c.C + c.A * s + n * c.R;
	}
	else
	{
		const float end = RefRandom() < 0.5 ? -1.0 : 1.0;
		const float z = 2.0 * RefRandom() - 1.0;
		const float phi = 2.0 * PI * RefRandom();
		const float ring = sqrt(max(0.0, 1.0 - z * z));
		n = vec3(ring * cos(phi), ring * sin(phi), z);
		if (dot(n, c.A) * end < 0.0)
			return false;
		x = c.C + c.A * (end * c.H) + n * c.R;
	}
	return dot(n, P - x) > 0.0;
}

// Where a ray from outside first meets a sphere, or a negative distance.
float RefHitSphere(vec3 C, float R, vec3 o, vec3 d)
{
	const vec3 oc = o - C;
	const float c2 = dot(oc, oc) - R * R;
	if (c2 <= 0.0)
		return -1.0;
	const float b = dot(oc, d);
	const float disc = b * b - c2;
	return disc < 0.0 ? -1.0 : -b - sqrt(disc);
}

// Where a ray from outside first meets a capsule, and the normal there.
float RefHitCapsule(GpuLight light, vec3 o, vec3 d, out vec3 n)
{
	const vec3 C = light.Position.xyz;
	const vec3 A = normalize(light.Extent.yzw);
	const float H = 0.5 * RefLampLength(light);
	const float R = light.Direction.w;
	const vec3 oc = o - C;
	const float oa = dot(oc, A);
	const vec3 op = oc - A * oa;
	if (dot(op, op) <= R * R && abs(oa) <= H)
		return -1.0;
	float best = 1.0e30;
	const float da = dot(d, A);
	const vec3 dp = d - A * da;
	const float a = dot(dp, dp);
	if (a > 1.0e-12)
	{
		const float b = dot(op, dp);
		const float c2 = dot(op, op) - R * R;
		const float disc = b * b - a * c2;
		if (disc >= 0.0)
		{
			const float t = (-b - sqrt(disc)) / a;
			if (t > 0.0 && abs(oa + t * da) <= H)
			{
				best = t;
				n = normalize(op + dp * t);
			}
		}
	}
	for (int e = 0; e < 2; ++e)
	{
		const float end = e == 0 ? -1.0 : 1.0;
		const vec3 centre = C + A * (end * H);
		const float t = RefHitSphere(centre, R, o, d);
		if (t > 0.0 && t < best)
		{
			const vec3 m = (o + d * t - centre) / R;
			if (dot(m, A) * end >= 0.0)
			{
				best = t;
				n = m;
			}
		}
	}
	return best < 1.0e30 ? best : -1.0;
}

// The nearest shaped lamp a segment passes through before `reach`: its index
// (-1 for none), where, and the normal there.
int RefCrossLamp(vec3 o, vec3 d, float reach, out vec3 x, out vec3 n)
{
	int found = -1;
	float best = reach;
	for (int i = 0; i < u_Scene.LightCount; ++i)
	{
		const GpuLight light = u_Lights.Lights[i];
		if (!RefLampShaped(light))
			continue;
		vec3 normal = vec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0);
		float t;
		if (RefLampLength(light) <= 0.0)
		{
			t = RefHitSphere(light.Position.xyz, light.Direction.w, o, d);
			normal = normalize(o + d * t - light.Position.xyz);
		}
		else
		{
			t = RefHitCapsule(light, o, d, normal);
		}
		if (t > 0.0 && t < best)
		{
			best = t;
			found = i;
			n = normal;
		}
	}
	if (found >= 0)
		x = o + d * best;
	return found;
}

// One lamp, chosen by its weight at this vertex, and its light toward P
// through whatever glass is in the way. A shaped lamp's point is weighed
// against the path finding the same light.
vec3 RefLampNee(RefHit h, vec3 V, float total)
{
	if (total <= 0.0)
		return vec3(0.0);
	const float pick = RefRandom() * total;
	int index = u_Scene.LightCount - 1;
	float running = 0.0;
	for (int i = 0; i < u_Scene.LightCount; ++i)
	{
		running += RefLampWeight(u_Lights.Lights[i], h.P);
		if (pick < running)
		{
			index = i;
			break;
		}
	}
	const GpuLight light = u_Lights.Lights[index];
	const float weight = RefLampWeight(light, h.P);
	if (weight <= 0.0)
		return vec3(0.0);
	const float chance = weight / total;

	vec3 L;
	float reach;
	vec3 arriving;
	float pdfLight = 0.0;
	if (!RefLampShaped(light))
	{
		const vec3 color = light.Color.rgb * light.Color.a;
		if (light.Position.w == 0.0)
		{
			L = -light.Direction.xyz;
			reach = 1.0e6;
			arriving = color;
		}
		else
		{
			const vec3 toLight = light.Position.xyz - h.P;
			const float distance2 = dot(toLight, toLight);
			reach = sqrt(max(distance2, 1.0e-8));
			L = toLight / reach;
			arriving = color * RefLampScale(light, h.P) / max(distance2, 0.0001);
		}
	}
	else if (RefLampLength(light) <= 0.0)
	{
		if (!RefSampleSphere(light.Position.xyz, light.Direction.w, h.P, L, reach, pdfLight))
			return vec3(0.0);
		arriving = RefLampRadiance(light, h.P);
	}
	else
	{
		const RefCapsule c = RefCapsuleFrom(light, h.P);
		vec3 x, n;
		if (!RefSampleCapsule(c, h.P, x, n))
			return vec3(0.0);
		const vec3 toX = x - h.P;
		reach = length(toX);
		L = toX / reach;
		const float cosL = dot(n, -L);
		if (cosL <= 0.0)
			return vec3(0.0);
		pdfLight = RefCapsuleAreaPdf(c, x) * reach * reach / cosL;
		arriving = RefLampRadiance(light, h.P);
	}
	const vec3 f = RefBsdfCos(h, V, L);
	if (all(equal(f, vec3(0.0))) || all(equal(arriving, vec3(0.0))))
		return vec3(0.0);
	const vec3 through = RefTransmittance(RefOffset(h.P, h.Ng), L, reach);
	if (all(equal(through, vec3(0.0))))
		return vec3(0.0);
	if (pdfLight <= 0.0)
		return f * arriving * through / chance;
	const float pl = chance * pdfLight;
	return f * arriving * through * RefPowerHeuristic(pl, RefBsdfPdf(h, V, L)) / pl;
}

// A shaped lamp the path met after the vertex at `from`, weighed against the
// light sample taken there.
vec3 RefLampCrossing(int index, vec3 x, vec3 n, vec3 direction, vec3 from, float pdfPath, float total)
{
	const GpuLight light = u_Lights.Lights[index];
	const vec3 emitted = RefLampRadiance(light, from);
	if (total <= 0.0)
		return emitted;
	const float chance = RefLampWeight(light, from) / total;
	float pdfLight = 0.0;
	if (RefLampLength(light) <= 0.0)
	{
		const float cone = RefSphereCone(light.Position.xyz, light.Direction.w, from);
		pdfLight = cone > 0.0 ? 1.0 / (2.0 * PI * cone) : 0.0;
	}
	else
	{
		const vec3 toX = x - from;
		const float cosL = abs(dot(n, direction));
		pdfLight = cosL > 1.0e-6 ? RefCapsuleAreaPdf(RefCapsuleFrom(light, from), x) * dot(toX, toX) / cosL : 0.0;
	}
	return emitted * RefPowerHeuristic(pdfPath, chance * pdfLight);
}

// --- glowing surfaces: the emissive triangles --------------------------------
//
// Every glowing instance's triangles, in world space (Renderer3D builds them
// once for the reference). A vertex chooses an instance in proportion to its
// emitted power over the square of its distance (never nearer than its own
// size), a triangle in it by area, a point on that uniformly, and reads the
// glow there exactly as a path meeting it would. Both sides glow, as the frame
// draws them. What the path meets is weighed against these samples (MIS) --
// except where no sample could have found it (glass, a posed mesh, or straight
// from the camera).

float RefEmitterWeight(RefEmitter e, vec3 P)
{
	const float power = RefLuminance(e.Radiance.rgb) * e.Radiance.w;
	const vec3 toC = e.Sphere.xyz - P;
	return power / max(dot(toC, toC), max(e.Sphere.w * e.Sphere.w, 1.0e-4));
}

float RefEmitterTotal(vec3 P)
{
	float total = 0.0;
	const int count = u_RefEmitters.Records.length();
	for (int i = 0; i < count; ++i)
		total += RefEmitterWeight(u_RefEmitters.Records[i], P);
	return total;
}

vec3 RefEmitterNee(RefHit h, vec3 V, float total)
{
	if (total <= 0.0)
		return vec3(0.0);
	const int count = u_RefEmitters.Records.length();
	const float pick = RefRandom() * total;
	int index = count - 1;
	float running = 0.0;
	for (int i = 0; i < count; ++i)
	{
		running += RefEmitterWeight(u_RefEmitters.Records[i], h.P);
		if (pick < running)
		{
			index = i;
			break;
		}
	}
	const RefEmitter e = u_RefEmitters.Records[index];
	const float weight = RefEmitterWeight(e, h.P);
	if (weight <= 0.0 || e.TriangleCount == 0u)
		return vec3(0.0);
	const float chance = weight / total;

	// The triangle, by the running area shares (a binary search), and a point
	// on it, uniform.
	const float u = RefRandom();
	uint lo = e.FirstTriangle;
	uint hi = e.FirstTriangle + e.TriangleCount - 1u;
	while (lo < hi)
	{
		const uint mid = (lo + hi) / 2u;
		if (u < u_RefTriangles.Records[mid].P0.w)
			hi = mid;
		else
			lo = mid + 1u;
	}
	const RefEmitterTriangle tri = u_RefTriangles.Records[lo];
	const float su = sqrt(RefRandom());
	const float v = RefRandom();
	const vec2 bary = vec2(su * (1.0 - v), su * v);
	const vec3 x = tri.P0.xyz + tri.E1.xyz * bary.x + tri.E2.xyz * bary.y;
	const vec3 face = cross(tri.E1.xyz, tri.E2.xyz);
	const float faceLength = length(face);
	if (faceLength <= 0.0)
		return vec3(0.0);
	const vec3 toX = x - h.P;
	const float dist2 = dot(toX, toX);
	const float dist = sqrt(dist2);
	const vec3 L = toX / dist;
	const float cosL = abs(dot(face / faceLength, L));
	if (cosL <= 1.0e-6)
		return vec3(0.0);
	const vec3 f = RefBsdfCos(h, V, L);
	if (all(equal(f, vec3(0.0))))
		return vec3(0.0);
	const vec3 glow = RefEmission(e.Row, floatBitsToUint(tri.E1.w), bary);
	if (all(equal(glow, vec3(0.0))))
		return vec3(0.0);
	// To just short of the glowing surface, which would otherwise stop its own light.
	const vec3 through = RefTransmittance(RefOffset(h.P, h.Ng), L, max(dist - max(2.0e-3, dist * 2.0e-5), 0.0));
	if (all(equal(through, vec3(0.0))))
		return vec3(0.0);
	// Per unit solid angle: the instance's chance over its area, through the
	// distance and the slope (the triangle's chance over its own area is one
	// over the instance's).
	const float pl = chance * dist2 / (e.Radiance.w * cosL);
	return f * glow * through * RefPowerHeuristic(pl, RefBsdfPdf(h, V, L)) / pl;
}

// What the path's own find of a glowing surface is worth beside the glowing
// samples taken at the vertex `from`.
float RefEmitterHitWeight(RefHit h, vec3 direction, vec3 from, float pdfPath, float total)
{
	if (pdfPath <= 0.0 || total <= 0.0)
		return 1.0;
	const uint k = u_RefRowEmitter.Rows[h.Instance];
	if (k == ~0u)
		return 1.0;
	const RefEmitter e = u_RefEmitters.Records[k];
	const float cosL = abs(dot(h.Ng, direction));
	if (cosL <= 1.0e-6 || e.Radiance.w <= 0.0)
		return 1.0;
	const vec3 d = h.P - from;
	const float chance = RefEmitterWeight(e, from) / total;
	return RefPowerHeuristic(pdfPath, chance * dot(d, d) / (e.Radiance.w * cosL));
}

// --- one path ---------------------------------------------------------------

vec3 RefPath(vec3 origin, vec3 direction)
{
	vec3 radiance = vec3(0.0);
	vec3 throughput = vec3(1.0);
	float width = 0.0;   // the cone's, at the segment's origin
	bool underWater = false;
	// The last vertex that chose its direction by a density (not glass's
	// straight-through or water's refraction): where it was, that density, and
	// the totals its light choices were made from -- what a lamp or a glowing
	// surface the path then meets is weighed against. A density of zero means
	// no light sample could have found it: the camera, or a refraction.
	vec3 lastPosition = origin;
	float lastPdf = 0.0;
	float lastLampTotal = 0.0;
	float lastEmitterTotal = 0.0;
	const int bounces = max(int(u_Ref.Settings.x + 0.5), 1);
	for (int bounce = 0; bounce <= bounces; ++bounce)
	{
		g_ViewDepthScale = bounce == 0 ? max(dot(direction, g_CameraForward), 0.0) : 1.0;
		RefHit h;
		const bool found = RefTrace(origin, direction, width, underWater ? REF_MASK_DRY : REF_MASK_ALL, h);

		// A lamp's shape this segment passes through before what it hits.
		if (lastPdf > 0.0)
		{
			vec3 x, n;
			const int lamp = RefCrossLamp(origin, direction, found ? h.Distance : 1.0e6, x, n);
			if (lamp >= 0)
				radiance += throughput * RefLampCrossing(lamp, x, n, direction, lastPosition, lastPdf, lastLampTotal);
		}
		if (!found)
		{
			radiance += throughput * RefSky(direction);
			break;
		}
		width += g_ConeSpread * h.Distance;
		// What glows, as the path meets it -- on a pane, only its surface
		// share, as the frame's blend scales the pane's whole colour by its
		// alpha -- weighed against the glowing samples at the last vertex.
		if (max(h.Emissive.r, max(h.Emissive.g, h.Emissive.b)) > 0.0)
			radiance += throughput * h.Emissive * (h.Glass ? h.Opacity : 1.0)
					  * RefEmitterHitWeight(h, direction, lastPosition, lastPdf, lastEmitterTotal);
		if (bounce == bounces)
			break;

		const vec3 V = -direction;

		// On water, the refracted ray first: how far it travels to the bottom
		// sets what the water lets through, which both the body's light and
		// the path below need.
		vec3 refracted = vec3(0.0);
		float caustic = 0.0;
		if (h.Water)
		{
			refracted = refract(direction, h.N, REF_WATER_ETA);
			const vec3 below = RefOffset(h.P, -h.Ng);
			const float through = dot(refracted, refracted) > 1.0e-6
								? RefNearest(below, refracted, REF_MASK_DRY) : -1.0;
			// Foam floats on the surface and hides the bottom (the frame's
			// transmittance times 1 - foam); the bottom it does let through
			// carries the caustic web at the point the refracted ray lands.
			h.WaterT = through >= 0.0 ? exp(-h.WaterSigma * through) * (1.0 - h.WaterFoam) : vec3(0.0);
			if (through >= 0.0)
				caustic = RefWaterCaustics(h.WaterPattern, (below + refracted * through).xz, through,
										   h.WaterGradient, h.WaterWind, h.WaterTime);
		}

		// One lamp and one glowing surface, each sampled here.
		const float lampTotal = RefLampTotal(h.P);
		const float emitterTotal = RefEmitterTotal(h.P);
		radiance += throughput * (RefLampNee(h, V, lampTotal) + RefEmitterNee(h, V, emitterTotal));

		// The next direction. Every choice that is not a delta is weighed by
		// the whole surface over the whole density (RefBsdfCos over
		// RefBsdfPdf), whichever sampler drew it; the deltas carry their own
		// share over their own chance.
		vec3 L;
		vec3 weight = vec3(1.0);
		int kind = 0;   // 0 drawn by a density, 1 straight through glass, 2 refracted into water
		if (h.Water)
		{
			float Fv, pReflect, pBottom;
			RefWaterChances(h, V, Fv, pReflect, pBottom);
			if (RefRandom() < pReflect)
			{
				L = RefSampleWater(h, V);
			}
			else if (RefRandom() < pBottom)
			{
				L = refracted;
				weight = (1.0 - Fv) * h.WaterT * (1.0 + caustic) / ((1.0 - pReflect) * pBottom);
				kind = 2;
			}
			else
			{
				L = RefSampleDiffuse(h);
			}
		}
		else if (h.Glass && RefRandom() >= h.Opacity)
		{
			if (RefRandom() < RefPaneReflectChance(h, V))
			{
				mat3 frame;
				float ax, ay;
				RefBaseLobe(h, frame, ax, ay);
				L = RefSampleLobe(frame, ax, ay, V);
			}
			else
			{
				// (1 - F) of the clear share passes, chosen with chance 1 - F:
				// the weight is one, the direction unchanged.
				L = direction;
				kind = 1;
			}
		}
		else
		{
			L = RefSampleSurfaceDirection(h, V);
		}
		float pdf = 0.0;
		if (kind == 0)
		{
			pdf = RefBsdfPdf(h, V, L);
			const vec3 f = RefBsdfCos(h, V, L);
			if (pdf <= 0.0 || all(equal(f, vec3(0.0))))
				break;
			weight = f / pdf;
		}
		throughput *= weight;

		// Russian roulette from the fourth vertex: unbiased, and it ends the
		// paths that no longer carry anything.
		if (bounce >= 3)
		{
			const float keep = clamp(max(throughput.r, max(throughput.g, throughput.b)), 0.05, 0.95);
			if (RefRandom() > keep)
				break;
			throughput /= keep;
		}
		if (kind == 0)
		{
			lastPosition = h.P;
			lastPdf = pdf;
			lastLampTotal = lampTotal;
			lastEmitterTotal = emitterTotal;
		}
		else if (kind == 2)
		{
			lastPdf = 0.0;
			underWater = true;
		}
		origin = RefOffset(h.P, kind != 0 ? -h.Ng : h.Ng);
		direction = L;
	}
	return radiance;
}

void main()
{
	const uvec2 pixel = uvec2(gl_FragCoord.xy);
	const uint samples = uint(u_Ref.Projection.w + 0.5);
	g_Rng = pixel.x * 1973u + pixel.y * 9277u + samples * 26699u + 0x6A09E667u;
	g_Rng = RefNext() ^ (samples * 0x9E3779B9u);

	// Anywhere inside the pixel, so the mean is the pixel's average and not
	// its centre's: a box filter, the reference's own anti-aliasing.
	const vec2 size = vec2(textureSize(u_ReferencePrevious, 0));
	const vec2 jitter = vec2(RefRandom(), RefRandom()) - 0.5;
	const vec2 uv0 = v_UV + jitter / size;
	const bool flip = u_Ref.Projection.z > 0.5;
	const vec2 uv = vec2(uv0.x, flip ? 1.0 - uv0.y : uv0.y);
	const vec3 frame = ViewPosition(uv, 1.0, u_Ref.Projection.xy);
	const vec3 view = normalize(vec3(frame.x, flip ? -frame.y : frame.y, -frame.z));
	const vec3 direction = normalize(vec3(dot(u_Ref.CameraRow0.xyz, view), dot(u_Ref.CameraRow1.xyz, view),
										  dot(u_Ref.CameraRow2.xyz, view)));

	// The cone: the pixel's angle, over the square root of the samples the
	// mean is heading for and never below an eighth of it -- the jittered
	// samples already average the pixel, so a footprint need only span the
	// spacing between them.
	g_CameraForward = -normalize(vec3(u_Ref.CameraRow0.z, u_Ref.CameraRow1.z, u_Ref.CameraRow2.z));
	const float pixelAngle = 2.0 * abs(u_Ref.Projection.y) / size.y;
	g_ConeSpread = pixelAngle * max(0.125, inversesqrt(max(u_Ref.Settings.z, 1.0)));

	// --reference-debug: a lane of the first surface in place of the light.
	vec3 radiance;
	const int debugLane = int(u_Ref.Settings.w + 0.5);
	if (debugLane != 0)
	{
		g_ViewDepthScale = max(dot(direction, g_CameraForward), 0.0);
		RefHit h;
		radiance = vec3(0.0);
		if (RefTrace(u_Ref.CameraPosition.xyz, direction, 0.0, REF_MASK_ALL, h))
		{
			if (debugLane == 1)
				radiance = h.Albedo;
			else if (debugLane == 2)
				radiance = vec3(max(dot(h.N, -direction), 0.0), 1.0, 0.0);
			else
				radiance = vec3(h.Roughness, h.Metallic, h.Water ? 3.0 : h.Glass ? 2.0 : 1.0);
		}
	}
	else
	{
		radiance = RefPath(u_Ref.CameraPosition.xyz, direction);
	}
	float invalid = 0.0;
	if (any(isnan(radiance)) || any(isinf(radiance)))
	{
		radiance = vec3(0.0);
		invalid = 1.0;
	}

	if (u_Ref.Settings.y > 0.5)
	{
		const vec4 previous = texelFetch(u_ReferencePrevious, ivec2(pixel), 0);
		// The mean over the valid samples, in full floats: a bad one is
		// counted in alpha and left out of the average, never averaged in as a
		// zero (which would darken exactly the pixels that have a bug).
		const float valid = float(samples) - previous.a;
		o_Mean = invalid > 0.0 ? vec4(previous.rgb, previous.a + 1.0)
							   : vec4(previous.rgb + (radiance - previous.rgb) / (valid + 1.0), previous.a);
	}
	else
	{
		o_Mean = vec4(radiance, invalid);
	}
}
